            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0235" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg111"/>

                <head>No. 84.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Titus to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1881-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 22, 1881</date>. (Received September 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The last coast mail brought a note from the
                    minister of foreign relations of Costa Rica in answer to the one sent him,
                    according to your instructions, by Mr. Logan, concerning the proposed
                    arbitration between Costa Rica and Colombia. I inclose a copy of the note
                    clipped from the official journal of Costa Rica, and a translation of the
                    same.</p>
                <p>As being calculated to throw some light on the views of the Costa Ricans on this
                    subject, I also inclose a translation of an article from the Mensajero, a
                    journal of San José, sent to the legation with the Gaceta Oficial, commenting
                    upon the notes.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRANK H. TITUS.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d84-a1.xml" xpointer="d84-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d84-a2.xml" xpointer="d84-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
